# TEST 37 — full RC mock, harder. Written after 동하's real 10/31 score came back (810: LC 445 / RC 365, about 73-75%
# correct in RC) while he was scoring ~88% on TEST 33-36: the mocks matched real length and vocabulary numbers but were
# too easy to answer. What makes the real test harder, and what this set does:
#  - P5 vocabulary distractors come from the same field and fit the grammar; sentence logic, a preposition, or a
#    fixed pattern decides (refrain FROM, compatible WITH, postpone ... UNTIL). More structure traps: p.p. tail vs main
#    verb, subject-verb agreement, subjunctive, inverted conditional, "those", "well ahead of".
#  - P6 blanks need the neighbouring sentences (tense, reference, connector, context vocabulary).
#  - P7 distractors are built from facts that ARE in the passage but twisted (wrong person, time, scope, direction), so
#    every option has to be checked; correct options are inferences or abstractions, not copies; idioms carry the
#    intent questions (see to that, that'll have to do, leave that to me); syntax is denser (inversion, participial
#    and concessive clauses). Cross-passage items stay single look-ups, as in the real tests.
DIVIDER_NOTE = "RC 실전 모의고사 (난이도 상향). 새로 작성한 연습 문제입니다. 실제 기출 문항이 아닙니다."
NATURAL_KEY = True
DOUBLE = [["p0", "p1"], ["q"]]
TRIPLE = [["p0", "p1"], ["p2", "q"]]

